+# AN-900: Record a consent for a person
+
+- **Jira:** AN-900
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2, 3)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:** <GitHub login> <YYYY-MM-DD>
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: other modules through the new event `identity.consent-changed`; `apps/worker` wires the consent store
+
+## Context
+
+Head office must prove each consent of a person, for example for marketing e-mails. The `identity` module owns consents (architecture section 4, T3-D-009).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+IDs only; `pnpm ids show <ID>` prints the text.
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| T3-AC-004 | `packages/core/src/identity/consent.test.ts`, `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** `createIdentity` takes `consents: ConsentRepository`. New methods `recordConsent({ personId, purpose, textVersion, channel, granted }): ConsentRecord` (throws `UnknownPersonError`; an error for an unknown channel), `currentConsent(personId, purpose): ConsentRecord | null`, `consentHistory(personId): ConsentRecord[]` (oldest first). New exports `InMemoryConsentRepository`, `UnknownPersonError`, types `ConsentRecord`, `ConsentChannel`, `ConsentRepository`, `ConsentChanged`, `RecordConsentInput`. New invariants: records are append-only; the channel is `web`, `advisor` or `import`. AC: T3-AC-004.
+- **Contracts:** new event `identity.consent-changed`, payload `consentId`, `personId`, `purpose` (IDs only; consumers read the decision with `currentConsent`). [ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-consent-changed-event.md). No ERP operation.
+- **Schema:** new table `identity.consent`:
+
+  | Column | Personal | Category | Purpose | Retention |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|
+  | `id` | no | | | |
+  | `person_id` (FK `identity.person`) | yes | identity | Link the decision to the person | account lifetime + 3 years |
+  | `purpose` | no | | | |
+  | `text_version` | no | | | |
+  | `channel` (`web`, `advisor`, `import`) | yes | preference | Proof of consent: where | account lifetime + 3 years |
+  | `granted` | yes | preference | Proof of consent: the decision | account lifetime + 3 years |
+  | `decided_at` | yes | preference | Proof of consent: when | account lifetime + 3 years |
+
+  Owner: `identity`. Index on (`person_id`, `purpose`). Existing categories only.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- T3-AC-004 "type" maps to `purpose`, "source" to `channel`, "date" to `decided_at`, "withdrawal" to a new record with `granted: false`. Mapping, not a change of the AC.
+- `purpose` is free text for now; no purpose catalogue is in scope.
+- The store interface has `append` and `listByPerson` only, so the code cannot change or delete a record.
+- The current decision is the latest record per person and purpose by `decided_at`; equal times keep insertion order.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Consent screens, the e-mail marketing tool interface, the migration of old consents (story scope).
+- A database-level guard against `UPDATE`/`DELETE` (grants or a trigger) and the Drizzle repository: they come with the first PostgreSQL adapter of `identity`.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Should a purpose catalogue (allowed purposes) be fixed in this module, or by the e-mail marketing integration?
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
